HST Office: "Cổ điển" is the LibreOffice Colibre icon set, with HST glyphs where Colibre has none.

Reason: the owner chose upstream Colibre as the classic icon style (sharp SVG on HiDPI), keeping
the colourful hst_modern as the default. The new hst_classic / hst_classic_dark archives (built by
scripts/brand/build-hst-icon-theme.py from the tree's own Colibre) hold only the HST glyphs for
icon requests Colibre does not resolve - the org.hst.office.vi commands, statistics dialogs and
others - and fall back to colibre_svg / colibre_dark_svg for everything else. Both are SVG-only,
so macOS rasterises them at the backing scale. The options page writes "hst_classic"; profiles
of earlier versions name the classic style "hst" / "hst_dark", which now selects hst_classic /
hst_classic_dark when installed (the hst themes remain as the fallback layer of hst_modern).
"hst_classic" follows the UI mode like "hst_modern". configure accepts and installs the two themes.

Applies after hst-icon-theme.patch, hst-icon-theme-hidpi-and-cache.patch and
hst-icon-theme-modern-default.patch.
Test: make CppunitTest_vcl_app_test (test_HstIconTheme, test_IconThemeSelector).
License: upstream files remain MPL-2.0.
